doi: "10.5281/zenodo.19767827"
abstract: "Procurement activities in multinational chemical companies are typically characterized by high levels of complexity and dynamic 
operational conditions. In many cases, noticeable discrepancies arise between formally defined procedures and their actual execution, which 
may lead to inefficiencies, longer processing times, and potential compliance risks within Procure-to-Pay (Pr2P) operations. Although process 
mining has become an effective technique for examining business processes, much of the existing research mainly concentrates on process 
discovery and provides limited support for integrated performance analysis and decision-making in real operational settings. To overcome 
this limitation, this study introduces a data-driven analytical framework that combines process mining techniques with performance evaluation 
and software-based decision support to improve transparency and operational efficiency in procurement management. Real event log data collected 
from a multinational chemical company are analyzed to identify the actual P2P workflow and assess its conformance with the reference process model. 
Process behavior is modeled using Petri Net and Business Process Model and Notation (BPMN), while synchronization-based conformance checking is 
employed to detect deviations, rework occurrences, and non-compliant executions. In addition, performance indicators such as cycle time and throughput 
time are evaluated to identify bottlenecks and operational delays. A software prototype developed in Python, integrating the PM4Py library 
and additional data analytics modules, is implemented to facilitate interactive process discovery, visualization, and performance assessment. 
The empirical findings reveal considerable deviations from the standard P2P workflow, with invoice-related activities particularly invoice receipt recording, 
invoice payment, and payment block removal identified as the primary sources of excessive processing time. 
Overall, the proposed framework provides actionable managerial insights and supports continuous monitoring, compliance evaluation, 
and data-driven improvement of procurement processes in large-scale industrial contexts."
keywords:
  - process mining
  - Purchase-to-pay process
  - Conformance checking
  - Performance analysis
  - Business process improvement
